# System - the obligation layer above ACS
#
# Companion decision tables to system.md, which is the governing
# specification for this layer.  There is no governing paper: the
# layers below are governed by Bracha87.txt and BKR94ACS.txt, the
# reliability discipline by SRC84.txt; this layer's rules are derived
# in system.md and captured here in dtc form so they are
# mutually exclusive and exhaustive by construction -- the property
# BKR94's arithmetic circuit had and an unbounded application stream
# lacks.
#
# Every rule here is DERIVED -- forced by the requirements (R1-R4;
# R4 = participant tolerance) and implementer obligations (O1-O5)
# recorded in system.md, which cites the derivation at each rule.  The R4 advance rule is
# ENCODED below: the join, maintain, and admit tables all gate on
# "possession of the prior round" and "tolerance elapsed".  The O2
# two-grain artifact rides the SERVE act (.want and .have); the O5
# maintenance birth and precedence are the maintain table; the O3
# adopt rule is documented in the witness-event section at the end
# and lives as a C guard in systemWitness -- an independent rule
# set deliberately kept out of this dispatch.  Deliberately
# CALLER-SIDE (system.md "Mechanization status"): the serve walk's
# concurrency cap and rotation, the cross-kind byte budget,
# PRESENT's byte staging and subset-witness retirement, and the
# R2b resume constraint.  Identifier and predicate translation,
# and the entry-point/discriminator decisions, live in
# systemToC.dtc; the implementation is system.[hc].
#
# Events and discriminator.  Four events drive this layer -- the
# first three through the merged dispatch, the witness event
# through its C guard; each event's wrapper applies only its own
# outputs and discards the rest, exactly as bracha87Fig1Input
# applies paper outputs and bracha87Fig1Bpr applies retry outputs
# from one merged dispatch:
#
#   act received      - an act for round R, verified within chain
#                       reach (O1), arrives.  R is the round the
#                       act's IDENTITY proves, never the round its
#                       byte names (C12: reach is bounded on both
#                       sides).  Traffic beyond reach AHEAD is not
#                       evidence: its sender still owes it, so it
#                       re-arrives on that sender's own retry
#                       cadence once reach extends.  A caller MAY
#                       hold it as a latency optimization; nothing
#                       in the calculus requires the hold, and an
#                       unbounded hold of ahead traffic would be
#                       the remote inflation lever the Byzantine
#                       notes' retention-budget claim excludes.
#                       Traffic beyond reach BEHIND is
#                       unverifiable for good -- reach never
#                       extends backward -- and its sender is
#                       already in the out-of-band territory
#                       RETAIN prices.  (The FRONTIER round's
#                       possession indications are the opposite
#                       case and MUST be held -- their carrier
#                       retires at quiescence; see
#                       systemReceived's C11 obligation, which
#                       C12 binds to identity.)  Applies:
#                       "deliver the act to the live instance",
#                       "record serve owed to the sender for R",
#                       "record participation owed for R".
#   launch opportunity - the process is free to start an instance;
#                       paced by the tick (a wire rate limit, never
#                       a correctness clock).  Applies:
#                       "join the oldest owed round",
#                       "maintain the next round",
#                       "admit the next round".
#   retention event   - a possession record changed for retained
#                       round R, or the retention budget is pressed.
#                       Applies: "release R".
#   witness event     - a served assertion for the frontier round,
#                       validated by the caller against its
#                       candidate composition (O3).  Applies the
#                       adopt rule (C guard; see the witness-event
#                       section at the end of this file).
#
# A possession indication riding an inbound act is recorded as an
# ingress side effect before the dispatch (reads following writes);
# the tables see the post-record state.  Serving, once owed, is
# walked and paced C-side; its per-process retirement is the
# possession record consulted below, its per-round retirement is
# release.
#
# Inputs (all are authenticated local facts; Byzantine analysis of
# each is in system.md):
#   "round R relative to self"    { R COMPLETE and retained,
#                                   R COMPLETE and released,
#                                   R is the live instance,
#                                   R not yet reached }
#                                 - with one instance at a time and
#                                   rounds taken in order, every R
#                                   is exactly one of these.
#                                   Traffic strictly ahead of the
#                                   frontier is refused BEFORE the
#                                   dispatch (beyond chain reach --
#                                   Model), so "R not yet reached"
#                                   is entered only by the frontier
#                                   round awaiting its join
#   "sender has evidenced possession of R"     { yes, no }
#   "own instance live"                        { yes, no }
#   "participation owed to any round"          { yes, no }
#   "application value pending"                { yes, no }
#   "own backlog drained"                      { yes, no }
#   "possession of the prior round"  { short of n-t,
#                                      at n-t, short of all n,
#                                      at all n, or not retained }
#                                 - composition possession of the
#                                   round below the frontier (the R4
#                                   advance signal); a round no
#                                   longer retained reads as met --
#                                   duty is bounded by retention
#   "tolerance elapsed"                        { yes, no }
#                                 - T_p sweeps of this process's own
#                                   re-offers since the n-t signal
#                                   (caller-counted, like the barren
#                                   sweeps that drive abandon)
#   "identity maintenance due"                 { yes, no }
#                                 - O5: authorship budget exhaustion
#                                   forces an identity-maintenance
#                                   round (caller fact, self-local)
#   "all n processes have evidenced possession of R"   { yes, no }
#   "retention budget exceeded"                { yes, no }
#   "R is the oldest retained round"           { yes, no }
#
# Outputs:
#   "deliver the act to the live instance"     { yes, no }
#   "record serve owed to the sender for R"    { yes, no }
#   "record participation owed for R"          { yes, no }
#   "join the oldest owed round"               { yes, no }
#   "maintain the next round"                  { yes, no }
#   "admit the next round"                     { yes, no }
#   "release R"                                { yes, no }
#
# (The O3 "adopt the frontier round" rule is documented in the
# witness-event section below and lives as a C guard -- an
# independent rule set kept out of this dispatch.)

# ================================================================
# Act received for round R
# ================================================================

# Delivery.  An act for the live instance's round feeds that
# instance; every other class of round has no live consumer.
@"deliver the act to the live instance","round R relative to self"
yes,"R is the live instance"
no,"R COMPLETE and retained"
no,"R COMPLETE and released"
no,"R not yet reached"

# SERVE birth (DERIVED -- system.md SERVE, two grains per O2: the
# act carries .want -- who is owed -- and .have -- which members'
# content this process can serve; composition serves always, held
# members beside it, and a member held nowhere reachable is a
# per-member out-of-band hole, never the round's failure).
# Want is observed, never inferred from
# self-need: an act of R from a process not recorded as possessing
# R is that process wanting R, and a completer that retains R owes
# it a serve.  A released round is out-of-band territory; a
# not-yet-reached round is not ours to serve.  The record is per
# (round, sender); re-arrivals while a serve is owed change
# nothing (the record is already made -- same shape as the sent
# flags one level down).
@"record serve owed to the sender for R","round R relative to self","sender has evidenced possession of R"
yes,"R COMPLETE and retained",no
no,"R COMPLETE and retained",yes
no,"R is the live instance",
no,"R COMPLETE and released",
no,"R not yet reached",

# PARTICIPATE birth (DERIVED -- system.md R2a: the papers' own
# participation premise makes this conformance, not policy).  Verified
# existence of a round this process has not reached obliges this
# process to take part: a round, once observed, is every correct
# process's obligation, whether or not this process has anything
# of its own to send.  Without this rule a drained process stops
# taking part and the tail of a sequence stalls below the n-t
# threshold.  The act itself is also held for delivery when the
# round is joined (C-side mechanics).
@"record participation owed for R","round R relative to self"
yes,"R not yet reached"
no,"R is the live instance"
no,"R COMPLETE and retained"
no,"R COMPLETE and released"

# ================================================================
# Launch opportunity
# ================================================================

# Owed work before chosen work (DERIVED).  Discharging an existing
# obligation outranks assuming a new one, and joining a round also
# enters this process's own pending value -- participation is
# contribution, so no value waits longer by joining than by
# admitting.  The oldest owed round is joined first (rounds are
# taken in order); selecting it is C-side enumeration driven by
# this go-signal.  The join is NOT gated on the backlog:
# capacity may defer only chosen work (M2); owed work is paced by
# the tick alone (M1 -- local state never defers discharge).  The
# join IS gated on the R4 advance rule -- tolerance governs joins
# exactly as admissions, else a process that launches the next
# round immediately voids every honest hold; bounded deferral
# preserves R2a's eventual participation.
@"join the oldest owed round","own instance live","participation owed to any round","possession of the prior round","tolerance elapsed"
no,yes,,,
yes,no,yes,"at all n, or not retained",
yes,no,yes,"at n-t, short of all n",yes
no,no,yes,"at n-t, short of all n",no
no,no,yes,"short of n-t",
no,no,no,,

# MAINTAIN (DERIVED -- system.md O5, ADMIT birth (b)).  Identity
# maintenance outranks the pending value and must not consume it:
# a maintenance round's win is not the value's win, so the
# contribution is the deployment's maintenance form, never the
# staged application value.  Chosen work, so it sits under the
# same self-capacity and R4 advance gates as ADMIT; owed work
# still outranks it.
@"maintain the next round","own instance live","participation owed to any round","identity maintenance due","own backlog drained","possession of the prior round","tolerance elapsed"
no,yes,,,,,
no,no,yes,,,,
no,no,no,no,,,
no,no,no,yes,no,,
yes,no,no,yes,yes,"at all n, or not retained",
yes,no,no,yes,yes,"at n-t, short of all n",yes
no,no,no,yes,yes,"at n-t, short of all n",no
no,no,no,yes,yes,"short of n-t",

# ADMIT (DERIVED -- system.md M2 + the R4 advance rule; O5
# precedence: maintenance outranks the value).  A
# process takes on the next round of its own volition only when
# nothing is owed, no maintenance is due, a value is pending, its
# own backlog has drained -- every result its prior advances
# accepted has reached its decision stream, the one capacity fact
# a blind transmitter can know: emission is a put on a carrier
# contracted to eventually drain (A4) and attests nothing beyond
# the attempt -- AND the
# prior round's duty is discharged: all n possess it (or it left
# retention), or n-t possess it and T_p sweeps of tolerance have
# funded the tail's catch-up.  Admitting while prior results sit
# undelivered, or while the tail's funded window still runs,
# is the defect class this gate exists to prevent: intake
# outrunning discharge until an honest process sheds from the
# sequence and the fault budget is spent on load.
@"admit the next round","own instance live","participation owed to any round","identity maintenance due","application value pending","own backlog drained","possession of the prior round","tolerance elapsed"
no,yes,,,,,,
no,no,yes,,,,,
no,no,no,yes,,,,
no,no,no,no,no,,,
no,no,no,no,yes,no,,
yes,no,no,no,yes,yes,"at all n, or not retained",
yes,no,no,no,yes,yes,"at n-t, short of all n",yes
no,no,no,no,yes,yes,"at n-t, short of all n",no
no,no,no,no,yes,yes,"short of n-t",

# ================================================================
# Witness event for the frontier round -- not in this dispatch
# ================================================================
#
# ADOPT (DERIVED -- system.md O3, the wanting side).  A served
# assertion the caller validated against its candidate composition
# accumulates one distinct-server witness (the record marks only
# its sender; self is not a server of its own adoption).  At t+1
# distinct servers at least one is honest, so the composition is
# acceptable: signal adoption exactly once:
#
#   adopt the frontier round  iff  post-record distinct witnesses
#   reach t+1 AND adoption is not already signaled.
#
# The caller then closes through the ONE consume region --
# systemComplete -- which a racing own COMPLETE enters first at
# most, superseding the book (the supersession is structural:
# complete clears the book either way).  Below threshold nothing
# is acted on: accumulating evidence is M1-protected state, not a
# fact.
#
# Kept OUT of the merged dispatch on the bkr94acs BPR-gate
# precedent: its two inputs appear in no other rule, so it is an
# INDEPENDENT rule set -- merging it would duplicate its DAG at
# every leaf of the launch/received rules for zero ordering
# insight (the decisionTableCompiler discipline: independent
# problems get separate dispatches; threshold-and-latch guards
# with no test-ordering question stay in C).  Implemented as the
# C early-output in systemWitness.

# ================================================================
# Retention event for round R
# ================================================================

# RELEASE (DERIVED -- system.md RETAIN/O4: release advances the
# derivation floor and the retention floor together).  A retained round releases when provably no
# correct process can still need it -- all n have evidenced
# possession (with at most t forgeries, reaching n requires every
# correct process's true indication; no count-threshold shortcut)
# -- or when the retention budget forces eviction, oldest retained
# round first.  Eviction under budget is the one place bounded
# memory overrides M1; the evicted round becomes out-of-band
# territory, which is the accept-loss boundary, not a protocol
# stop.
@"release R","all n processes have evidenced possession of R","retention budget exceeded","R is the oldest retained round"
yes,yes,,
yes,no,yes,yes
no,no,yes,no
no,no,no,
